{"help": "https://catalogue.data.govt.nz/api/3/action/help_show?name=package_show", "success": true, "result": {"author": "Ministry of Health", "author_email": "", "creator_user_id": "5ff73065-c758-4327-9f5e-8d0ebee52611", "frequency_of_update": "", "id": "97a16c27-3bb7-4ea7-88b3-fe7f36bfff53", "isopen": true, "issued": "2023-06-29", "language": "", "license_id": "CC-BY-4.0", "license_title": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International", "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "maintainer": "Health Survey", "maintainer_email": "healthsurvey@health.govt.nz", "maintainer_phone": "", "metadata_created": "2025-07-02T01:18:00.097007", "metadata_modified": "2025-07-02T01:21:45.203387", "modified": "2023-06-29", "name": "racial-discrimination-2011-12-2016-17-and-2020-21-new-zealand-health-survey", "notes": "A racial discrimination module has been included in the adult New Zealand Health Survey questionnaire intermittently. This report contains data from the last three modules included in the 2011/12, 2016/17 and 2020/21 New Zealand Health Survey. It presents information on how adults in New Zealand experience racial discrimination, including through ethnically motivated personal attack (physical or verbal), and unfair treatment in health care, employment or housing.\r\n\r\nData is available on people\u2019s experience of racial discrimination over 2 time periods: in the 12 months before the survey and over their lifetime. Results are also shown by ethnic group for M\u0101ori, Pacific, Asian and non-M\u0101ori/non-Pacific/non-Asian people.", "num_resources": 3, "num_tags": 2, "organization": {"id": "adde14b1-f9ea-467d-b0eb-cd78d24afbf3", "name": "ministry-of-health", "title": "Ministry of Health", "type": "organization", "description": "The Ministry of Health \u2013 Manat\u016b Hauora is the chief steward of New Zealand\u2019s health system and the lead advisor to Government on health. Our core responsibilities are policy, monitoring, and regulati